# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build context for the ROOT Dockerfile (render.yaml: dockerContext: .)
#
# Docker only reads a .dockerignore at the context root, so the two nested
# ones (pathwise/, pathwise-backend/) do nothing for the production image —
# this file is what actually applies to it.
#
# The important entry is node_modules. Both stages run `npm ci` and then
# `COPY <half>/ ./` on top; without this, a host tree built on Windows or
# macOS is layered over the Linux install, and the platform-specific binaries
# npm resolved (rollup, esbuild, swc) are the wrong ones. That fails at build
# time with a missing-module error that has nothing to do with the code.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets must never enter an image layer. Vite inlines anything VITE_* it
# finds at build time, so a stray pathwise/.env would be baked into the bundle
# the browser downloads.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test output and local noise.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright
**/*.log

# Not needed to build, and .git is large.
.git
.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
